From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the shell may lock the pointer over a window

A game or VM viewer asks the compositor to lock the pointer
(zwp_pointer_constraints_v1), and the engine draws and moves the pointer,
so the lock is the shell's to take: a pointer lock on the window's <app>,
after which the element hears only relative motion.

Chrome's delegate sends the request to the exclusive-access manager, which
wants a click first and draws a "Press Esc to exit" bubble. A desktop
locks for a client that asked, with no click in between, and shows no
browser UI, so the shell window's delegate grants the lock outright. The
shell decides when to take it and when to let go.

WRITTEN BY HAND, AGAINST THE SERIES RATHER THAN IN A CHECKOUT, so its
post-image blob is not known and is left zeroed, as 0036's is.
---
 .../browser_web_contents_delegate.cc                | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_web_contents_delegate/browser_web_contents_delegate.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_web_contents_delegate/browser_web_contents_delegate.cc
index 2f8a419..0000000 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_web_contents_delegate/browser_web_contents_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_web_contents_delegate/browser_web_contents_delegate.cc
@@ -413,12 +413,16 @@
 void BrowserWebContentsDelegate::RequestPointerLock(
     content::WebContents* web_contents,
     bool user_gesture,
     bool last_unlocked_by_target) {
-  exclusive_access_manager_->pointer_lock_controller()->RequestToLockPointer(
-      web_contents, user_gesture, last_unlocked_by_target);
+  // Domicile: the shell locks the pointer over a window whose client asked it
+  // to, which no click need precede, and Chrome's "Press Esc to exit" bubble
+  // is browser UI the desktop draws none of. The shell decides when to lock
+  // and when to let go; this only grants it.
+  web_contents->GotResponseToPointerLockRequest(
+      blink::mojom::PointerLockResult::kSuccess);
 }
 
 void BrowserWebContentsDelegate::LostPointerLock() {
-  exclusive_access_manager_->pointer_lock_controller()
-      ->ExitExclusiveAccessToPreviousState();
+  // Domicile: nothing to put back, since the grant above never went through
+  // the exclusive-access manager.
 }
